repository-code: "https://github.com/queelius/openai-math-counterexamples"
abstract: >-
  Independent exact verification of the explicit degree-three cocycle and
  twisted boundary identities in OpenAI's Family 199 construction, using
  two polynomial implementations, complete finite basis coverage and
  meaningful failure controls. The full Auslander-Reiten counterexample
  theorem is outside scope. OpenAI supplied the construction and table;
  Pico supplied the preceding starting-algebra check. Substantial OpenAI
  Codex assistance and a separate AI review are disclosed. Included source
  snapshots and transcribed source data retain Apache-2.0 attribution.
